	&fw->data[4 + sizeof(struct ti_i2c_image_header)],
	le16_to_cpu(img_header->Length));
Reason:
The function allocates a fixed-size heap buffer (`buffer_size` = (16*1024 - 512) + sizeof(struct ti_i2c_firmware_rec)) but then copies `le16_to_cpu(img_header->Length)` bytes into it without verifying that the length fits in the remaining space after the firmware record header. Since `img_header->Length` is a `__le16` from the firmware file (up to 65535), it can far exceed `buffer_size`, causing a heap buffer overflow.

