		buffer_size - sizeof(struct ti_i2c_firmware_rec)) {
	kfree(buffer);
	return -EINVAL;
}
Reason:
This check validates that the image header length does not exceed the available destination buffer space (after the firmware record header) before the `memcpy`. If it exceeds, the allocated buffer is freed and an error is returned, preventing the heap overflow.

